erial insufficiency or vascular occlusion. 2. DIGITAL BLOOD FLOW TEST Purpose To assess circulation to the fingers. Procedure • • Compress the fingertip until it blanches. Release the pressure. Positive Sign Delayed capillary refill (>2 seconds). Indicates Reduced peripheral circulation. 3. FIGURE-OF-8 MEASUREMENT Purpose To assess hand and wrist swelling (edema). Procedure • Use a measuring tape in a standardized figure-of-8 pattern around the wrist and hand. Record the measurement. 1 • Positive Finding Increased measurement compared with the opposite side. Indicates Hand or wrist edema. 4. HAND VOLUME TEST Purpose To assess ha\n<truncated 891 bytes>\n5. Assessment - Demographic Data. Chief complaint, History of Present illness including functional limitation, Past Medical Surgical history, Family history, Occupational & Personal history, Socio-Economic, Environmental and Psychological History, Drug and Treatment History etc. Musculoskeletal Disorders:Vital parameters (Temperature, Respiratory Rate, Peripheral Pulses, Blood Pressure). Body Built of Patient, Artitude of Limb, Bony contours, Deformities, Trophic changes.\r\nExamination of Posture. Examination of Spasm, Tenderness, Edema /swelling/wasting including Limb girth measurement. Scar examination. Motor Examination: Range of Motion, Joint Play & End Feel, Muscle Strength, Power, Endurance, Flexibility, Isometric Resisted Testing, Limb-length discrepancy, Pelvic inclination, Examination of Balance, Gait & External aids/assistive Device used etc. Sensory Examination: Superficial & Deep sensation, Reflexes, Dermatomes, and Myotomes etc.((Dermatomes\r\nDefinition: Areas of skin supplied by sensory fibers fro\n<truncated 4495 bytes>\n6. put dots where ever reqried to know its new line example this types of dots ;  structures • Images\n7. 1. Neck Disability Index (NDI)\n• Definition and Overview\n• Developed by Howard Vernon and Silvano Mior in 1991 as a modification of the Oswestry Low Back Pain Disability Questio